# Record Version Info in Skills

When writing or updating a `SKILL.md`, always record the specific version(s)
of the application, infrastructure, or platform the skill was written
against (e.g. OpenShift 4.22, RHOAI 3.5, a specific operator channel/CSV
version, a tool's major.minor version).

- State versions explicitly near the top of the skill (overview or first
  relevant step), not buried in a footnote.
- If the skill covers a range of supported versions, state the range and
  which version was actually verified.
- If a behavior, flag, or manifest differs across versions, call that out
  rather than silently documenting only the current one.
- Prefer commands that let the reader confirm the version on their own
  cluster/environment (e.g. `oc version`, `oc get clusterversion`,
  `oc get csv -n <namespace>`) over hardcoding a version with no
  verification path.
